---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Page title="Terms of use" kicker="Legal" description="The terms for using Equator Ledger, a free travel blog about Ecuador and the Galápagos published by Tourground." path="/terms/">
  <p>By using {SITE.url.replace('https://', '')} (“the site”) you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>The site is published by Tourground (“we”, “us”). Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  <h2>2. What the site is</h2>
  <p>The site is a free travel blog. We do not sell travel, take bookings, handle payments or act as anyone’s agent. Any contract you make is between you and the company you book with.</p>
  <h2>3. Information, not advice</h2>
  <p>We write carefully and cite our sources, but the site gives general information, not legal, medical, financial or travel advice. Entry rules, health requirements, park fees and safety advice change. Check important facts with the official sources we cite, and with your operator, before you book or travel.</p>
  <h2>4. No endorsement</h2>
  <p>Mentioning a place, authority or company is not a guarantee. Paid content, if any, is labelled “Advertisement feature” and kept separate from editorial content. See our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>5. Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>We link to operators, official sources and other websites. We are not responsible for their content, availability or practices.</p>
  <h2>6. Reusing our content</h2>
